flowchart TB
    accTitle: How an owner gets a release app
    accDescr: You copy the blueprint with the question of the release app left empty. The checklist links the registration of the app on your account or organization, with its name and permissions filled in. You create the app and its private key, and name it with copier update and the name, Client ID and App ID of its settings page. After the commit, settings apply sets the variables and the ruleset of the release tags, and the checklist asks for the private key and the installation on the repository. Then the bots run as your app; until then each bot that acts as it says in its summary what is missing.

    copy(["copier copy<br>release app left empty"])
    link["`**checklist**<br>a link registers the app<br>name and permissions filled in`"]
    app(["You create the app<br>and its private key"])
    named["`**copier update --data release_app=…**<br>name, Client ID, App ID`"]
    apply["`**settings apply**<br>variables and the ruleset<br>of the release tags`"]
    key(["The private key in the<br>environment release,<br>the app installed"])
    bots["The bots run<br>as your app"]
    waiting["Until then: the summary<br>of each bot says<br>what is missing"]

    copy --> link --> app --> named --> apply --> key --> bots
    copy -.-> waiting

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class link,named,apply,waiting bot
    class copy,app,key person
    class bots done
